The key part is the loop that renders the `ContextMenuItem` components:

```javascript
{filteredContextMenuActions.map((contextAction, index) => {
    // ...
    return (
        <ContextMenuItem
            // ...
            onPress={(event) =>
                contextAction.onPress(
                    closePopup,
                    {...payload, ...transactionPayload},
                    event as GestureResponderEvent | MouseEvent,
                )
            }
            // ...
        />
    );
})}
```

The `onPress` handler for each `ContextMenuItem` is calling `contextAction.onPress`. This means I need to go back to `ContextMenuActions.tsx` and modify the `onPress` functions for "Copy to clipboard", "Copy link", and "Mark as unread".

